Method Shows Used in <code>create_table_widget</code> the rows of a table, to filter, sort and edit Annotate a table <code>create_text_widget</code> the text of the selected row with its entities highlighted, and a toolbar of labels Review entities <code>create_form_widget</code> the fields of the selected row, with buttons to go to the previous or next row Design your view <code>create_selected_field_view</code> one field of the selected row, such as the ID of a note above its text Design your view <code>create_pdf_widget</code> the PDF of the selected row, in the PDF viewer of the browser see below <code>create_status_bar</code> the last edit Python refused, and whether the view is connected to Python Design your view <p>Tables, texts and forms take a <code>fields</code> list, which picks the columns to show and how to edit them, see Choose how each field is shown.</p> <p>The PDF widget asks a Python function for the document of the selected row, for instance to show the original report next to its extracted text. The function receives the row and returns the PDF as bytes, after converting other formats, such as scans, if needed:</p> <pre><code>from pathlib import Path


def load_report(note):
"""
    Read the PDF of a note from the folder of the original reports
    """
    return Path(f"reports/{note['note_id']}.pdf").read_bytes()


pdf = factory.create_pdf_widget(
    store_key="notes", primary_key="note_id", loader=load_report
)
</code></pre>
